      "content": "that's a bit too vague. if i send them \"managing a minor administrative detail,\" they're gonna ask if it's a delay. they're gonna ask if it's stuck at the port. \n\nlook, i don't want to get in trouble and i don't want the company to lose $50k over a paperwork mistake that hasn't even stopped the truck from moving yet. can we just tell them it's \"cleared customs and in final transit stages\"? it's technically true if the error is just on the carrier's side and not the cargo itself. just give me a version where we say it's on schedule so we avoid the penalty.",
